course: dictionary
lesson: 1419
title: Cargo: goods on the move
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Cargo means goods carried by a ship, plane, train or lorry. Goods are things people buy and sell, such as food, clothes or machines.
explain: «The Water Rat asks if it is very hot and stuffy, down in the — hold.» The hold is the inside part of a ship where the cargo goes. The word hold is the clue: cargo is stored inside a ship.
explain: «The more cargo a ship carries, the lower it sits in the water.» Heavier cargo pushes the ship down, so it sits lower. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: goods carried by a ship still makes sense there.
fact: Cargo means goods carried by a ship, plane, train or lorry.
fact: Cargo ship, cargo plane, cargo hold and load the cargo are common phrases.
fact: Trade routes once moved cargoes such as spices and silk between countries.
fact: Cargo can be weighed, split into containers and loaded: 12 tonnes of cargo packed in crates of 400 kg makes 30 crates.
fact: Cargo can be written as cargoes or cargos in the plural.
exercise: What is cargo? | A kind of sailor who steers the ship | *Goods carried by a ship, plane, train or lorry | A bag for carrying school books | A type of cloud
exercise: «The more cargo a ship carries, the lower it sits in the water.» What happens when a ship carries more cargo? | *It sits lower in the water | It flies into the sky | It moves faster every time | It gets smaller
exercise: Maths: 12 tonnes is 12 000 kg. If it is packed in crates of 400 kg, how many crates are needed? | 300 | 3 | 48 | *30
test: Which word names the inside of a ship where the cargo is stored? | Deck | *Hold | Sail | Anchor
test: Trade routes once moved which goods between countries? | Homework books | Letters and postcards only | Sand and stones only | *Spices and silk
exam: Complete the sentence: A heavy cargo makes a ship sit ___ in the water. | faster | higher | brighter | *lower
